# Change an exercise. Start the API with Aspire first, then send the first three requests once.
@host = http://localhost:5279

### Create an account → 201. The requests below use its access token.
# @name createAccount
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user-{{$guid}}@example.com",
  "password": "password",
  "timeZone": "Europe/Zagreb"
}

### The groups → 200. A new account's groups can take a moment to appear.
# @name groups
GET {{host}}/api/v1/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create an exercise → 201. The requests below use it.
# @name createExercise
POST {{host}}/api/v1/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bench press",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"
}

### New values → 200.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/{{createExercise.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Incline bench press",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[1].id}}",
  "alsoWorksGroupIds": ["{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"]
}

### Another exercise's name → 409 exercise.name_taken, once a second exercise has it.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/{{createExercise.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pull-up",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"
}

### An exercise that does not exist → 404 exercise.not_found.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/exercises/0198a000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{createAccount.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Pull-up",
  "groupId": "{{groups.response.body.$[0].id}}"
}
